    "['match ip address prefix-list [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'from policy-options policy-statement policy1 term 10 match route-filter 0.0.0.0/0 upto /32', 'parent_command': ['set protocols ospf import [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set protocols ospf import [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nfrom policy-options policy-statement policy1 term 10 match route-filter 0.0.0.0/0 upto /32\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Cisco `match ip address prefix-list ALL` matches routes against the prefix-list named \"ALL\"\\n- The equivalent Juniper command uses `route-filter` under policy-statement terms\\n- The prefix-list \"ALL\" in Cisco permits all routes (0.0.0.0/0 le 32), which translates to `0.0.0.0/0 upto /32` in Juniper\\n- The command is placed within a policy-statement term context, maintaining the same policy name \"policy1\" and term number \"10\" for consistency', 'trans_template': 'from policy-options policy-statement policy1 term 10 match route-filter 0.0.0.0/0 upto /32'}]]": 1,
